→ expect 401.\n\n## 2. Folders\n\n### 2.1 Create a folder (root)\n- **Behavior**: `POST /folders` with `{ name }` creates a top-level folder. Returns `201` and `{ id, name, parentId: null, ownerId, createdAt }`.\n- **Verify**: Auth'd POST to `/folders` with `{ name: \"Root\" }` → 201, response has `id`, `name: \"Root\"`, `parentId: null`.\n\n### 2.2 Create a nested folder\n- **Behavior**: `POST /folders` with `{ name, parentId }` creates a child folder. Returns `201` with `parentId` set.\n- **Verify**: Create root folder, then POST child with `parentId` = root's id → 201, parentId matches.\n\n### 2.3 Create folder validates name\n- **Behavior**: Missing name returns `400`.\n- **Verify**: POST `/folders` with `{}` → 400.\n\n### 2.4 Create folder with non-existent parent\n- **Behavior**: `parentId` referencing a non-existent folder returns `404`.\n- **Verify**: POST `/folders` with `parentId: \"nonexistent\"` → 404.\n\n### 2.5 Get folder by ID\n- **Behavior**: `GET /folders/:id` returns the folder with `200` and full details.\n- **Verify**: Create folder, GET it → 200, body matches.\n\n### 2.6 Get non-existent folder\n- **Behavior**: `GET /folders/:id` for missing id returns `404`.\n- **Verify**: GET with random id → 404.\n\n### 2.7 Update folder name\n- **Behavior**: `PATCH /folders/:id` with `{ name }` updates the folder. Returns `200` with updated folder. Only owner can update.\n- **Verify**: Create folder as owner, PATCH with new name → 200, name changed.\n\n### 2.8 Delete folder (owner only)\n- **Behavior**: `DELETE /folders/:id` deletes the folder. Returns `204`. Only owner can delete.\n- **Verify**: Create folder as owner, DELETE → 204. GET afterward → 404.\n\n### 2.9 Delete folder with nested content\n- **Behavior**: Deleting a folder also deletes all nested documents and sub-folders.\n- **Verify**: Create parent → child folder → document in child. DELETE parent → 204. GET child → 404. GET document → 404.\n\n### 2.10 Non-owner cannot update/delete folder\n- **Behavior**: A user who is not the folder owner (and not an editor/shared owner) gets `403` on PATCH or DELETE.\n- **Verify**: User A creates folder. User B auths and tries PATCH/DELETE → 403.\n\n## 3. Documents\n\n### 3.1 Create document in folder\n- **Behavior**: `POST /folders/:folderId/documents` with `{ title, content }` creates a document. Returns `201` with `{ id, title, content, folderId, ownerId, createdAt }`.\n- **Verify**: Create folder, POST document to it → 201, response has all fields.\n\n### 3.2 Create document validates required fields\n- **Behavior**: Missing title or content returns `400`.\n- **Verify**: POST with `{}`, `{ title }`, `{ content }` → each returns 400.\n\n### 3.3 Create document in non-existent folder\n- **Behavior**: Invalid folderId returns `404`.\n- **Verify**: POST to `/folders/bad/documents` → 404.\n\n### 3.4 Get document by ID\n- **Behavior**: `GET /documents/:id` returns the document with `200`.\n- **Verify**: Create document, GET it → 200, body matches.\n\n### 3.5 Get non-existent document\n- **Behavior**: `GET /documents/:id` for missing id returns `404`.\n- **Verify**: GET random id → 404.\n\n### 3.6 Update document\n- **Behavior**: `PATCH /documents/:id` with `{ title, content }` updates. Returns `200` with updated document. Owner or editor can update.\n- **Verify**: Create doc as owner, PATCH title+content → 200, both updated.\n\n### 3.7 Delete document (owner only)\n- **Behavior**: `DELETE /documents/:id` deletes. Returns `204`. Only owner can delete.\n- **Verify**: Create doc, DELETE → 204. GET → 404.\n\n### 3.8 Non-owner/editor cannot update document\n- **Behavior**: A viewer-only user gets `403` on PATCH.\n- **Verify**: User A creates doc, shares as viewer with B. User B tries PATCH → 403.\n\n### 3.9 Non-owner cannot delete document\n- **Behavior**: A non-owner (even editor) gets `403` on DELETE.\n- **Verify**: User A creates doc, shares as editor with B. User B tries DELETE → 403.\n\n## 4. Sharing & Permissions\n\n### 4.1 Share folder with another user\n- **Behavior**: `POST /share/folder/:folderId` with `{ userId, role }` shares a folder. Role is one of `viewer`, `editor`, `owner`. Returns `200` with share details. Only owner or editor can share.\n- **Verify**: User A creates folder, shares with B as viewer → 200.\n\n### 4.2 Share document with another user\n- **Behavior**: `POST /share/document/:documentId` with `{ userId, role }` shares a document. Returns `200`.\n- **Verify**: User A creates doc, shares with B as editor → 200.\n\n### 4.3 Share with invalid role\n- **Behavior**: Invalid role (not viewer/editor/owner) returns `400`.\n- **Verify**: Share with role \"admin\" → 400.\n\n### 4.4 Share with non-existent user\n- **Behavior**: Non-existent userId returns `404`.\n- **Verify**: Share with random userId → 404.\n\n### 4.5 Non-owner/editor cannot share\n- **Behavior**: A viewer user gets `403` when trying to share.\n- **Verify**: User A creates folder, shares with B as viewer. B tries to share with C → 403.\n\n### 4.6 Effective permission inheritance (folder→document)\n- **Behavior**: When a user is a viewer on a folder, they can read documents inside it.\n- **Verify**: A creates folder + document. A shares folder with B as viewer. B can GET the document → 200.\n\n### 4.7 Most permissive role when shared multiple ways\n- **Behavior**: User who is viewer on folder but editor on document gets effective editor on document.\n- **Verify**: A creates folder + doc. Shares folder with B as viewer, shares doc with B as editor → B can PATCH doc (editor permission).\n\n### 4.8 Viewer cannot update document in shared folder\n- **Behavior**: Viewer on folder can read but not update documents.\n- **Verify**: A creates folder + doc. Shares folder with B as viewer. B tries PATCH doc → 403.\n\n### 4.9 Editor on folder can update documents\n- **Behavior**: Editor on folder can read and update documents inside.\n- **Verify**: A creates folder + doc. Shares folder with B as editor. B PATCHes doc → 200.\n\n### 4.10 Editor on folder can share the folder\n- **Behavior**: Editor on a folder can share it with others (but cannot delete).\n- **Verify**: A creates folder, shares with B as editor. B shares folder with C as viewer → 200.\n\n### 4.11 Remove share\n- **Behavior**: `DELETE /share/:resourceType/:id/:userId` removes a share. Returns `204`. Only owner can remove shares.\n- **Verify**: A creates folder, shares with B. A removes share → 204. B can no longer access.\n\n### 4.12 Non-owner cannot remove share\n- **Behavior**: Non-owner gets `403` when trying to remove a share.\n- **Verify**: A creates folder, shares with B as editor. B tries to remove A's share → 403.\n\n## 5. Activity Log\n\n### 5.1 Get activity log\n- **Behavior**: `GET /activity` returns an array of activity log entries. Each entry has `actionType`, `userId`, `targetType`, `targetId`, `timestamp`.\n- **Verify**: Register A, create folder, create doc. GET /activity → array with entries for folder creation, doc creation.\n\n### 5.2 Log documents creation\n- **Behavior**: Creating a document logs `DOCUMENT_CREATE`.\n- **Verify**: Create doc → log contains entry with `actionType: \"DOCUMENT_CREATE\"`.\n\n### 5.3 Log document updates\n- **Behavior**: Updating a document logs `DOCUMENT_UPDATE`.\n- **Verify**: Create + update doc → log contains `DOCUMENT_UPDATE`.\n\n### 5.4 Log document deletion\n- **Behavior**: Deleting a document logs `DOCUMENT_DELETE`.\n- **Verify**: Create + delete doc → log contains `DOCUMENT_DELETE`.\n\n### 5.5 Log sharing events\n- **Behavior**: Sharing a resource logs `SHARE_CREATE`. Removing share logs `SHARE_REMOVE`.\n- **Verify**: Share a folder → log has `SHARE_CREATE`. Remove share → log has `SHARE_REMOVE`.\n\n### 5.6 Log entries are ordered by timestamp\n- **Behavior**: Activity log entries are in chronological order (oldest first).\n- **Verify**: Perform several actions, GET /activity → timestamps are non-decreasing.\n\n## 6. General\n\n### 6.1 `createApp()` exported\n- **Behavior**: Main module exports `createApp()` function returning Express app.\n- **Verify**: Import and call `createApp()` → returns an Express app instance.\n\n### 6.2 TypeScript compiles\n- **Behavior**: `npm run build` succeeds with no errors.\n- **Verify**: Run the command → exit code 0, no stderr.\n\n### 6.3 ESLint passes\n- **Behavior**: `npm run lint` passes with no errors.\n- **Verify**: Run the command → exit code 0, no errors.\n\n### 6.4 All tests pass\n- **Behavior**: `npm test` runs vitest and all tests pass.\n- **Verify**: Run the command → exit code 0, all tests green.\n\n### 6.5 Data resets between server starts\n- **Behavior**: Each `createApp()` call starts with fresh state (no persistence).\n- **Verify**: Create data in one app instance, create a new instance → the new one has no data.\n\n## 7. Edge Cases\n\n### 7.1 Empty folders listing\n- **Behavior**: Getting a folder returns its children with no assumptions about order.\n- **Verify**: Create empty folder, GET it → response includes children arrays that are empty.\n\n### 7.2 Document content can be empty string\n- **Behavior**: Document content can be an empty string (but must be present).\n- **Verify**: Create doc with `content: \"\"` → 201. GET it → content is `\"\"`.\n\n### 7.3 Owner is automatically creator\n- **Behavior**: Creator of a resource is automatically its owner.\n- **Verify**: A creates folder. Check shares/owner field → A is owner.\n\n### 7.4 Self-share is rejected\n- **Behavior**: Sharing a resource with yourself returns `400`.\n- **Verify**: A creates folder, tries to share with self → 400.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
